<title>FRANCE: CIC H1 results seen up sharply - paper.</title>
<headline>CIC H1 results seen up sharply - paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>CIC, the banking unit of French state-owned insurer GAN, should post a half-year net attributable profit of more than 500 million francs, up nearly 40 percent from the year-earlier period, the French daily Le Monde reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Net attributable profit of the group should be more than 500 million francs for the first six months, representing a rise of nearly 40 percent,&quot; the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The government has announced plans to sell 67 percent of CIC (Credit Industriel et Commercial).</p>
<p>The bank is due to release its results later today.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
